                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8453f6ff-00f8-43ac-ac1e-7213bedabdc5",
                                "sense_id": "c1b08922-1448-34cb-adac-2fb6234466d3",
                                "text": "Оди́н стари́нный социо́лог смотре́л на вся́кую дурну́ю страсть как на си́лу, кото́рую при уме́нье мо́жно напра́вить к добру́, а у нас и благоро́дная, краси́вая страсть зарожда́ется и пото́м вымира́ет как бесси́лие, никуда́ не напра́вленная, не по́нятая и́ли опо́шленная.",
                                "translation": "One of the early sociologists regarded every evil passion as a force which might by judicious management be turned to good, while among us even a fine, noble passion springs up and dies away in impotence, turned to no account, misunderstood or vulgarised.",
                                "english": "One of the early sociologists regarded every evil passion as a force which might by judicious management be turned to good, while among us even a fine, noble passion springs up and dies away in impotence, turned to no account, misunderstood or vulgarised."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
